{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"eeb5d6a6-a386-420c-b7da-436b24baaec4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I couldn’t finish the fix because I keep hitting a tool‑usage error (the tool expects either text **or** a tool call, not both). I’ll need to step back, review what’s wrong, and then re‑apply the needed edits in a clean way.\n\n**What I’ve found so far**\n\n| Issue | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **LaunchAgent points to the original home directory** | `ProgramArguments` in `com.vk.nightly-review.plist` uses `/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh`. The script lives at `/tmp/h‑HLKeOQ/bin/nightly-review.zsh`. |\n| **Log file paths are wrong** | `StandardOutPath` and `StandardErrorPath` point to `/Users/vk/Library/Logs/...`, but the snapshot stores logs under `/tmp/h‑HLKeOQ/Library/Logs/...`. |\n| **Script uses a read‑only variable** | The script sets `status=$?` even though `set -u` makes `status` read‑only, causing “read‑only variable: status” errors in the log. |\n| **Script now uses `exit_status` but still references `status`** | After renaming the variable, the `if` test still checks `$status`, so the error persists. |\n\n**Next steps**\n\n1. Update the plist to reference the correct script path.\n2. Update the plist to use the snapshot log paths.\n3. Ensure the script consistently uses the renamed `exit_status` variable.\n4. Reload the launch agent (`launchctl unload … \u0026\u0026 launchctl load …`) to verify it runs.\n\nI’ll restart the edit process in a single, validated step once the tool error is resolved. If you’d like me to proceed, just let me know.\n","duration_seconds":139.468279,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":42598,"output_tokens":13788,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":721792,"total_tokens":56386}}}
